6,0.028893696,-0.012719703,-0.033355486,0.022668777,-0.007380846,-0.0131694805,0.007479797,0.006287887,-0.0009900724,0.00012839737,-0.022003107,0.029217536,0.013439346,-0.057139713,-0.004461791,-0.042854782,-0.0027211527,-0.015247451,0.008338871,-0.0391846,-0.0049880305,-0.029991152,0.04692077,-0.027418425,0.02355034,-0.01926846,0.029199544,0.00823992,-0.039292548,-0.0023253488,0.04821613,-0.04379032,-0.03459687,-0.04274684,0.03886076,-0.00031259525,0.043070678,-0.023118554,0.014914616,-0.021283463,-0.030189054,0,0.00078992144,0.002203909,-0.0066342154,0.034093123,-0.04033603,0.00806001,0.025673289,-0.05253399,0.012656734,-0.008649218,-0.025547352,0.030063117,-0.02355034,-0.0010294279,0.007236917,-0.016668748,0.053577475,0.014338901,-0.01284564,0.016515823,0.011793162]	The diagram models a “ship‑goods” process. It begins with the activity “Ware soll versendet werden versenden” (initiate shipment). A parallel split then routes the flow to two branches: one proceeds to an exclusive decision that chooses among three shipping options – ordinary post, special shipment, or a default path. Selecting “Postversand” loops back to the parallel split, allowing repeated handling. Choosing “Sonder‑versand” triggers “Angebote einholen”, “günstigstes Angebot auswählen” and “Spediteur beauftragen” to obtain and award a carrier quote. The default path leads to “Paketschein ausfüllen” (fill shipping label). After the label is completed, another exclusive gateway asks whether insurance is required; if so, “Versicherung abschließen” is performed before both paths reconverge. The process then continues in parallel: one line moves to “Ware verpacken” (package the goods) while the other proceeds through a parallel gateway to “Ware bereitstellen” (make the goods available). Both branches ultimately converge and flow to the end event, completing the shipment preparation.	{"id": "__bung_1_920e781ac88741f18ff6143eacad5539", "source": "/app/bpmn_examples/__bung_1_920e781ac88741f18ff6143eacad553