se\\" isItalic=\\"false\\" isStrikeThrough=\\"false\\" isUnderline=\\"false\\" name=\\"Arial\\" size=\\"11.0\\"/>\\n      </bpmndi:BPMNLabelStyle>\\n      <bpmndi:BPMNLabelStyle id=\\"sid-db67e9af-351c-4ba1-8461-835c7081d1ee\\">\\n         <omgdc:Font isBold=\\"false\\" isItalic=\\"false\\" isStrikeThrough=\\"false\\" isUnderline=\\"false\\" name=\\"Arial\\" size=\\"12.0\\"/>\\n      </bpmndi:BPMNLabelStyle>\\n   </bpmndi:BPMNDiagram>\\n</definitions>\\n", "bpmn_model_description": "The diagram models a “ship‑goods” process. It begins with the activity “Ware soll versendet werden versenden” (initiate shipment). A parallel split then routes the flow to two branches: one proceeds to an exclusive decision that chooses among three shipping options – ordinary post, special shipment, or a default path. Selecting “Postversand” loops back to the parallel split, allowing repeated handling. Choosing “Sonder‑versand” triggers “Angebote einholen”, “günstigstes Angebot auswählen” and “Spediteur beauftragen” to obtain and award a carrier quote. The default path leads to “Paketschein ausfüllen” (fill shipping label). After the label is completed, another exclusive gateway asks whether insurance is required; if so, “Versicherung abschließen” is performed before both paths reconverge. The process then continues in parallel: one line moves to “Ware verpacken” (package the goods) while the other proceeds through a parallel gateway to “Ware bereitstellen” (make the goods available). Both branches ultimately converge and flow to the end event, completing the shipment preparation."}
