\\"sid-3BC3853B-A0F5-460E-857D-91393C90B84E_gui\\">\\n            <omgdi:waypoint x=\\"740.0\\" y=\\"380.0\\"/>\\n            <omgdi:waypoint x=\\"740.0\\" y=\\"369.0\\"/>\\n            <omgdi:waypoint x=\\"615.0\\" y=\\"369.0\\"/>\\n            <omgdi:waypoint x=\\"615.0\\" y=\\"280.0\\"/>\\n         </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>\\n         <bpmndi:BPMNEdge bpmnElement=\\"sid-3B019B12-DCEB-4BE3-8409-1198ECD335D6\\" id=\\"sid-3B019B12-DCEB-4BE3-8409-1198ECD335D6_gui\\">\\n            <omgdi:waypoint x=\\"200.0\\" y=\\"255.0\\"/>\\n            <omgdi:waypoint x=\\"200.0\\" y=\\"380.0\\"/>\\n            <omgdi:waypoint x=\\"105.0\\" y=\\"380.0\\"/>\\n            <omgdi:waypoint x=\\"105.0\\" y=\\"477.0\\"/>\\n         </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>\\n         <bpmndi:BPMNEdge bpmnElement=\\"sid-29B5FFEF-284F-416D-9682-58223F586469\\" id=\\"sid-29B5FFEF-284F-416D-9682-58223F586469_gui\\">\\n            <omgdi:waypoint x=\\"590.0\\" y=\\"495.0\\"/>\\n            <omgdi:waypoint x=\\"590.0\\" y=\\"180.0\\"/>\\n         </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>\\n      </bpmndi:BPMNPlane>\\n      <bpmndi:BPMNLabelStyle id=\\"sid-db6d4e8e-c386-40dc-b241-2c40100eae52\\">\\n         <omgdc:Font isBold=\\"false\\" isItalic=\\"false\\" isStrikeThrough=\\"false\\" isUnderline=\\"false\\" name=\\"Arial\\" size=\\"11.0\\"/>\\n      </bpmndi:BPMNLabelStyle>\\n      <bpmndi:BPMNLabelStyle id=\\"sid-62820b34-ff19-46d7-9987-cdf826cd84cc\\">\\n         <omgdc:Font isBold=\\"false\\" isItalic=\\"false\\" isStrikeThrough=\\"false\\" isUnderline=\\"false\\" name=\\"Arial\\" size=\\"12.0\\"/>\\n      </bpmndi:BPMNLabelStyle>\\n   </bpmndi:BPMNDiagram>\\n</definitions>\\n", "bpmn_model_description": "The diagram models a credit‑scoring service involving three participants: a Banking Front‑end, the Bank’s core system, and a Credit‑Protection Agency (CPA). The front‑end sends a “request score” message to the Bank, which starts the Bank process. The Bank asks the CPA for a score; this request is sent as a message to the CPA.  \\n\\nAt the CPA, a decision “Quick Scoring?” determines the flow. If a quick score is possible, the CPA immediately sends a **Level 1** score back to the Bank; otherwise it sends a **Delay Notice**, then performs a longer **Level 2** scoring routine and finally sends the Level 2 result.  \\n\\nThe Bank receives either a Level 1 score or a delay notice. In both cases it executes a “Display to Clerk” task, then waits for a Level 2 score. Once the Level 2 score arrives, the two scores converge at an exclusive gateway, the Bank presents the final result to the front‑end, and the process ends. This sequence orchestrates asynchronous score provision, optional delays, and a clerk’s review before delivering the final credit decision."}
