.451474e-05,-0.031799983,0.0014673198,0.03178157,0.056381904,0.012696056,0.015006941,0.027030908,-0.009349416,-0.0049347975,-0.0129078105,-0.007494264,0.0736537,-0.03522488,-0.056529213,0.0030980585,-0.014021822,-0.019941738,-0.032812722,-0.003553791,0.03060311,-0.00824461,0.036440168,0.009446086,0.03973617,-0.047985382,-0.013193218,0.0019276553,0.008985751,-0.044450007,-0.020880824,0.058701996,0.017170519,-0.04124607,-1.4331542e-05,0.023513943,0.009749908,0.009860389,0.028688114,0.007761258,0.0023477115,-0.00014270404,-0.024471441,-0.0039980146,-0.010716612,0.020254767,0.025613073,-0.022096109,-0.002137108,-0.0017630854,0.0055378373,-0.025410526,-0.0348382,-0.024287306,-0.015043767,-0.015227902,0.025981342,0.019260442,-0.011351876,0.030474218,-0.002238382,-0.037471317,0.001479979,0.047617115]	The model shows a credit‑inquiry workflow between a Customer and a Credit Company. The Customer sends a request (message flow) that triggers the Credit Company’s start event, where the company first **collects the applicant’s credit information**. That data is examined to see whether the requested amount is **≤ $1 million**; if it is, the case proceeds to a **risk‑assessment task**. The assessment leads to an exclusive gateway: when the risk is **low**, the process follows the “low‑risk” path to an **accept‑credit‑inquiry task** and ends with a message back to the Customer confirming acceptance. When the risk is **high** (or when the amount exceeds $1 million, which also routes directly to the high‑risk branch), the workflow moves to a **request‑approval task**. After the approval request, another gateway decides the outcome: if the credit is **rejected**, a **reject‑credit‑inquiry task** is performed and the process ends with a rejection message to the Customer; if the credit is **accepted**, the flow returns to the low‑risk gateway and continues to the acceptance task as above. Both final end events contain message‑event definitions, indicating that the Customer receives a notification of either approval or rejection. The external service provider participant appears in the collaboration but is not involved in the depicted flow.	{"id": "Credit_V3", "source": "/app/bpmn_examples/CoherenceCheckingDataset/Credit/Credit_V3.bpmn", "bpmn_model_xml": "<?xml version=\\"1.0\\" encoding=\\"UTF-8\\"?>\\n<bpmn:definitions xmlns:xsi=\\"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance\\" xmlns:bpmn=\\"http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/MODEL\\" xmlns:bpmndi=\\"http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/DI\\" xmlns:dc=\\"http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DC\\" xmlns:di=\\"http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DI\\" id=\\"Definitions_1\\" targetNamespace=\\"http://bpmn.io/schema/bpmn\\">\\n  <bpmn:collaboration id=\\"Collaboration_0bxs64x\\">\\n    <bpmn:participant id=\\"Participant_18pu9vn\\" name=\\"Credit Company\\" processRef=\\"Process_1\\" />\\n    <bpmn:participant id=\\"Participant_1qxes44\\" name=\\"Customer\\" />\\n    <bpmn:participant id=\\"Participant_1ixovqu\\" name=\\"external service provider\\" />\\n    <bpmn:messageFlow id=\\"MessageFlow_12roltb\\" sourceRef=\\"Participant_1qxes44\\" targetRef=\\"StartEvent_1\\" />\\n    <bpmn:messageFlow id=\\"MessageFlow_0l58mwt\\" sourceRef=\\"EndEvent_1s7qs5r\\" targetRef=\\"Participant_1qxes44\\" />\\n    <bpmn:messageFlow id=\\"MessageFlow_16d3xy5\\" sourceRef=\\"EndEvent_0kx7upr\\" targetRef=\\"Participant_1qxes44\\" />\\n  </bpmn:collaboration>\\n  <bpmn:process id=\\"Process_1\\" isExecutable=\\"false\\">\\n    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id=\\"ExclusiveGateway_16093oy\\">\\n      <bpmn:incoming>SequenceFlow_1elzcle</bpmn:incoming>\\n      <bpmn:outgoing>SequenceFlow_07674l9</bpmn:outgoing>\\n      <bpmn:outgoing>SequenceFlow_0w9d3cq</bpmn:outgoing>\\n    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>\\n    <bpmn:task id=\\"Task_1uq1q6f\\" name=\\"Assess risk&#10;\\">\\n      <bpmn:incoming>SequenceFlow_07674l9</bpmn:incoming>\\n      <bpmn:outgoing>SequenceFlow_0ba2jj4</bpmn:outgoing>\\n    </bpmn:task>\\n    <bpmn:exclusive