s2b_di\\" bpmnElement=\\"Participant_1qxes44\\">\\n        <dc:Bounds x=\\"123\\" y=\\"-94\\" width=\\"1214\\" height=\\"115\\" />\\n      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>\\n      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id=\\"Participant_0vnc16q_di\\" bpmnElement=\\"Participant_1ixovqu\\" isHorizontal=\\"true\\">\\n        <dc:Bounds x=\\"123\\" y=\\"500\\" width=\\"1217\\" height=\\"60\\" />\\n        <bpmndi:BPMNLabel />\\n      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>\\n      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id=\\"MessageFlow_12roltb_di\\" bpmnElement=\\"MessageFlow_12roltb\\">\\n        <di:waypoint x=\\"223\\" y=\\"21\\" />\\n        <di:waypoint x=\\"223\\" y=\\"106\\" />\\n        <bpmndi:BPMNLabel>\\n          <dc:Bounds x=\\"238\\" y=\\"57\\" width=\\"0\\" height=\\"13\\" />\\n        </bpmndi:BPMNLabel>\\n      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>\\n      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id=\\"MessageFlow_0l58mwt_di\\" bpmnElement=\\"MessageFlow_0l58mwt\\">\\n        <di:waypoint x=\\"1199\\" y=\\"106\\" />\\n        <di:waypoint x=\\"1199\\" y=\\"21\\" />\\n        <bpmndi:BPMNLabel>\\n          <dc:Bounds x=\\"1214\\" y=\\"57\\" width=\\"0\\" height=\\"13\\" />\\n        </bpmndi:BPMNLabel>\\n      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>\\n      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id=\\"MessageFlow_16d3xy5_di\\" bpmnElement=\\"MessageFlow_16d3xy5\\">\\n        <di:waypoint x=\\"1278\\" y=\\"281\\" />\\n        <di:waypoint x=\\"1278\\" y=\\"21\\" />\\n        <bpmndi:BPMNLabel>\\n          <dc:Bounds x=\\"1293\\" y=\\"144.5\\" width=\\"0\\" height=\\"13\\" />\\n        </bpmndi:BPMNLabel>\\n      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>\\n    </bpmndi:BPMNPlane>\\n  </bpmndi:BPMNDiagram>\\n</bpmn:definitions>\\n", "bpmn_model_description": "The model shows a credit‑inquiry workflow between a Customer and a Credit Company. The Customer sends a request (message flow) that triggers the Credit Company’s start event, where the company first **collects the applicant’s credit information**. That data is examined to see whether the requested amount is **≤ $1 million**; if it is, the case proceeds to a **risk‑assessment task**. The assessment leads to an exclusive gateway: when the risk is **low**, the process follows the “low‑risk” path to an **accept‑credit‑inquiry task** and ends with a message back to the Customer confirming acceptance. When the risk is **high** (or when the amount exceeds $1 million, which also routes directly to the high‑risk branch), the workflow moves to a **request‑approval task**. After the approval request, another gateway decides the outcome: if the credit is **rejected**, a **reject‑credit‑inquiry task** is performed and the process ends with a rejection message to the Customer; if the credit is **accepted**, the flow returns to the low‑risk gateway and continues to the acceptance task as above. Both final end events contain message‑event definitions, indicating that the Customer receives a notification of either approval or rejection. The external service provider participant appears in the collaboration but is not involved in the depicted flow."}
