.025883364,-0.020011075,0.00038673385,-0.011097492,-0.030946797,0.0006228184,0.01244828,0.030008525,-0.0027622401,-0.025786301,0.065355495,-0.011243086,-0.043613467,-0.030574724,-0.002262772,0.0133299325,-0.022874422,-0.008404004,-0.03630142,0.004038209,-0.020464035,0.034813125,0.036139645,0.049728412,-0.008581953,0.041381028,-0.03516902,-0.0006647778,0.0025034065,0.028309928,-0.034166038,-0.054516833,0.013896131,0.06988508,0.019897835,0.02373181,0.065679036,-0.009835678,0.0057752253,0.005661986,-0.0099165635,-0.0113967685,0.028617295,0.0250098,-0.02434654,-0.024718612,-0.0009923641,0.034068976,-0.008767989,0.036657315,-0.008581953,-0.03371308,-0.013524057,-0.013936574,0.010757773,0.026514271,0.03717498,0.0046913596,-0.025090685,-0.035104312,0.035298437,0.0023375913]	The diagram models a patient‑care pathway inside the **Hospital** pool. It begins with a **Start** event and the task **“Examine patient.”** An exclusive gateway asks whether an additional exam is needed. If **No**, the flow proceeds straight to a gateway that leads to **“Release patient”** and ends the case. If **Yes**, the process orders an examination and follow‑up treatment, then **“Inform about risks.”** A second decision checks whether the patient agrees to the plan; a **Yes** branches to **“Make appointment,”** then to **“Prepare examination.”** After preparation a gateway decides whether the examination can continue; the positive branch leads to **“Take sample.”** The sample step splits in parallel: **“Perform follow‑up treatment”** and **“Send sample.”** After both complete, the sample is **validated** and an exclusive gateway evaluates its quality. If the sample is OK, it is **analysed**, the **results are validated**, a **diagnosis is made**, and **therapy is described** before reaching the final end event. If the sample is not OK, a **send task “Report bad Sample”** notifies the **Medical Association** (via a message flow) and the process returns to the validation gateway for a re‑try. Throughout the path, a **calendar data store** records the appointment and a **doctor’s referral** document is produced when therapy is described. This flow captures decision‑points, parallel activities, and error handling for sample quality within the hospital’s treatment process.	{"id": "Hospital_V3", "source": "/app/bpmn_examples/CoherenceCheckingDataset/Hospital/Hospital_V3.bpmn", "bpmn_model_xml": "<?xml version=\\"1.0\\" encoding=\\"UTF-8\\"?>\\n<bpmn2:definitions xmlns:xsi=\\"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance\\" xmlns:bpmn2=\\"http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/MODEL\\" xmlns:bpmndi=\\"http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/DI\\" xmlns:dc=\\"http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DC\\" xmlns:di=\\"http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DI\\" id=\\"_XnkzIJtIEeWMdP0wHEPnRw\\" targetNamespace=\\"http://activiti.org/bpmn\\" exporter=\\"Camunda Modeler\\" exporterVersion=\\"1.0.0\\" xsi:schemaLocation=\\"http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/MODEL BPMN20.xsd\\">\\n  <bpmn2:dataStore id=\\"DataStore_1\\" name=\\"Data Store 1\\" />\\n  <bpmn2:collaboration id=\\"Collaboration_0if8286\\">\\n    <bpmn2:participant id=\\"Participant_120l3yn\\" name=\\"Hospital\\" processRef=\\"Process_1\\" />\\n    <bpmn2:participant id=\\"Participant_1vwct25\\" name=\\"Medical Association\\" />\\n    <bpmn2:messageFlow id=\\"Flow_09ot2cn\\" sourceRef=\\"Activity_1xzia0z\\" targetRef=\\"Participant_1vwct25\\" />\\n  </bpmn2:collaboration>\\n  <bpmn2:process id=\\"Process_1\\" isExecutable=\\"false\\">\\n    <bpmn2:laneSet />\\n    <bpmn2:sequenceFlow id=\\"SequenceFlow_1fi03yt\\" sourceRef=\\"pGate1\\" targetRef=\\"Task8\\" />\\n    <bpmn2:sequenceFlow id=\\"SequenceFlow_123c4er\\" sourceRef=\\"pGate1\\" targetRef=\\"Task9\\" />\\n    <bpmn2:sequenceFlow id=\\"SequenceFlow_1c8nzc8\\" sourceRef=\\"Task8\\" targetRef=\\"pGate2\\" />\\n    <bpmn2:sequenceFlow id=\\"SequenceFlow_1wji12c\\" sourceRef=\\"Task9\\" targetRef=\\"pGate2\\" />\\n    <bpmn2:sequenceFlow id=\\"flow19\\" name=\\"\\" 