0315435,0.0036216786,-0.017167727,0.0046085687,-0.023260098,-0.012952065,0.07721317,0.006989123,-0.003956805,0.017454319,-0.010788766,0.002926002,0.04548477,-0.016539076,0.013164697,0.0085561285,-0.037977934,0.011870415,-0.031617463,0.001137697,-0.040714417,-0.0029421805,-0.034760717,-0.013183187,-0.0062402883,0.0546187,0.027068984,0.026366374,-0.027808575,0.050366063,-0.03614745,-0.031672932,-0.05321348,-0.0022176136,-0.022557488,-0.0046155024,0.029491141,0.06656308,0.034705248,0.00063616276,-0.013266391,-0.014569918,0.017334135,0.024850216,-0.028585143,0.0021817898,-0.034390923,0.019931944,-0.024406461,0.03953107,-0.0020176934,0.05203014,-0.03683157,0.047222804,-0.0034437147,-0.044338405,-0.04481914,0.005727198,0.0037418618,0.0018431963,-0.00315019,0.028085921,-0.021207735,-0.035611246,-0.027272372,0.016816422]	The model shows three interacting pools – Visitor, Zoo (with ZooClub, Marketing and Billing lanes) and Bank. A visitor starts by deciding whether to buy an individual or family ticket, prepares the appropriate personal data, and sends this information to the Zoo’s ZooClub department. The ZooClub receives the message, records the visitor’s details and then, in parallel, forwards the data to Marketing and sends a billing request to the Billing lane. Marketing simply logs the request, while Billing creates a payment request that is sent to the Bank. The Bank processes the payment information and then charges the visitor’s account. Once the Bank confirms the charge, a “payment‑confirmed” message returns to the ZooClub, which then delivers the ZooClub card to the visitor. The visitor, after being told the card has been sent, waits for the card, receives a “card‑received?” message, confirms receipt and finishes the process. Parallel gateways synchronize the two parallel branches (marketing and billing) before the payment‑confirmation step, and the overall flow ends with the visitor’s successful card receipt.	{"id": "Zoo_v2", "source": "/app/bpmn_examples/Coherenc