92,0.009491745,0.02357886,0.027010337,0.019465102,-0.014307853,0.006170638,-0.01782963,-0.0030326426,0.060402017,-0.0012197043,-0.0033587334,0.02121094,-0.020568792,-0.04571289,-0.026970202,0.023819664,0.008277684,0.01105698,-0.027612349,-0.028555505,-0.0032182636,0.0013996812,-0.0020706754,-0.0062910407,-0.013414866,-0.0038604112,0.025324699,0.029017048,0.023538725,-0.017990168,-0.025966847,0.001739568,-0.017337987,-0.038368322,-0.009978373,0.02281631,-0.04535168,-0.05133168,-0.0013520218,0.045793157,0.004444866,0.034033827,0.00014062658,-0.00028736735,0.037645906,0.0019878985,-0.040736243,0.01856208,0.0054281545,-0.017057048,0.028354833,0.036883358,0.0034816444,0.009020168,-0.051291544,0.022013625,0.040395103,-0.0051146057,-0.025585571,0.0041438593,-0.020237686,-0.02191329,-0.004941527,0.008322836,0.020368122,-0.07276336,0.024983557,0.033772953]	The process models how the Provision Team fulfills a part‑supply request from a Customer. The Customer sends an initial request (a message‑triggered start event) and the team first **identifies the required parts**. An exclusive gateway then decides whether additional information must be gathered; if so a sub‑process “Elicit information from customer” is performed before checking stock. The **availability check** (using the RPDB datastore) leads to a second decision point: when the part is in stock the team **records the customer’s details**, orders and receives the part from the external supplier Daisuki (sub‑process “Order and receive part from Daisuki”), and then **contracts the customer**; when the part is not available the team proceeds directly to **supply the customer** with whatever is on hand. Both paths converge at a gateway that leads to **parts collection**, followed by **payment processing**, after which the process ends. Message flows link the Customer to the start, information‑gathering, parts‑collected and payment activities, and link Daisuki to the ordering sub‑process.	{"id": "Parts_V3", "source": "/app/bpmn_examples/CoherenceCheckingDataset/Replacement Parts/Parts_V3.bpmn", "bpmn_model_xml": "<?xml version=\\"1.0\\" encoding=\\"UTF-8\\"?>\\n<bpmn:definitions xmlns:xsi=\\"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance\\" xmlns:bpmn=\\"http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/MODEL\\" xmlns:bpmndi=\\"http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/DI\\" xmlns:dc=\\"http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DC\\" xmlns:di=\\"http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DI\\" id=\\"Definitions_1\\" targetNamespace=\\"http://bpmn.io/schema/bpmn\\">\\n  <bpmn:collaboration id=\\"Collaboration_0j223me\\">\\n    <bpmn:participant id=\\"Participant_0264ueb\\" name=\\"Provision Team\\" processRef=\\"Process_1\\" />\\n    <bpmn:participant id=\\"Participant_0ykebe4\\" name=\\"Customer\\" />\\n    <bpmn:participant id=\\"Participant_0fxuytk\\" name=\\"Daisuki\\" />\\n    <bpmn:messageFlow id=\\"MessageFlow_01f9pj4\\" sourceRef=\\"Participant_0ykebe4\\" targetRef=\\"StartEvent_1\\" />\\n    <bpmn:messageFlow id=\\"MessageFlow_0urhxn0\\" sourceRef=\\"Participant_0ykebe4\\" targetRef=\\"Task_17cgph5\\" />\\n    <bpmn:messageFlow id=\\"MessageFlow_0zwrtbt\\" sourceRef=\\"Task_17cgph5\\" targetRef=\\"Participant_0ykebe4\\" />\\n    <bpmn:messageFlow id=\\"MessageFlow_05t8wi2\\" sourceRef=\\"Task_0t7zeo2\\" targetRef=\\"Participant_0ykebe4\\" />\\n    <bpmn:messageFlow id=\\"MessageFlow_0v9cfqm\\" sourceRef=\\"Participant_0ykebe4\\" targetRef=\\"Task_05qpn5f\\" />\\n    <bpmn:messageFlow id=\\"MessageFlow_11hfz47\\" sourceRef=\\"Participant_0ykebe4\\" targetRef=\\"Task_0rkh5tz\\" />\\n    <bpmn:messageFlow id=\\"MessageFlow_0a2uzlz\\" sourceRef=\\"Participant_0fxuytk\\" targetRef=\\"Task_09m2tmj\\" />\\n    <bpmn:messageFlow id=\\"MessageFlow_047a914\\" sourceRef=\\"Task_09m2tmj\\" targetRef=\\"Participant_0fxuytk\\" />\\n  </bpmn:collaboration>\\n  <bpmn:process id=\\"Process_1\\" isExecutable=\\"false\\">\\n    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id=\\"SequenceFlow_1sqbuon\\" sourceRef=\\"StartEvent_1\\" targetRef=\\"Task_163w852