    <dc:Bounds x=\\"1672.5\\" y=\\"265\\" width=\\"0\\" height=\\"13\\" />\\n        </bpmndi:BPMNLabel>\\n      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>\\n      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id=\\"SequenceFlow_0fr19zm_di\\" bpmnElement=\\"SequenceFlow_0fr19zm\\">\\n        <di:waypoint x=\\"1814\\" y=\\"287\\" />\\n        <di:waypoint x=\\"1880\\" y=\\"287\\" />\\n        <bpmndi:BPMNLabel>\\n          <dc:Bounds x=\\"1847\\" y=\\"265.5\\" width=\\"0\\" height=\\"13\\" />\\n        </bpmndi:BPMNLabel>\\n      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>\\n      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id=\\"SequenceFlow_1ej0akn_di\\" bpmnElement=\\"SequenceFlow_1ej0akn\\">\\n        <di:waypoint x=\\"1980\\" y=\\"287\\" />\\n        <di:waypoint x=\\"2046\\" y=\\"287\\" />\\n        <bpmndi:BPMNLabel>\\n          <dc:Bounds x=\\"2013\\" y=\\"265\\" width=\\"0\\" height=\\"13\\" />\\n        </bpmndi:BPMNLabel>\\n      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>\\n      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id=\\"SequenceFlow_1mq5h5j_di\\" bpmnElement=\\"SequenceFlow_1mq5h5j\\">\\n        <di:waypoint x=\\"359\\" y=\\"120\\" />\\n        <di:waypoint x=\\"1356\\" y=\\"120\\" />\\n        <bpmndi:BPMNLabel>\\n          <dc:Bounds x=\\"824\\" y=\\"98\\" width=\\"68\\" height=\\"27\\" />\\n        </bpmndi:BPMNLabel>\\n      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>\\n    </bpmndi:BPMNPlane>\\n  </bpmndi:BPMNDiagram>\\n</bpmn:definitions>\\n", "bpmn_model_description": "The diagram models an invoice‑processing pipeline for a single participant called “Invoice Process”. It begins with a check — “Vendor located in SAP system”. If the vendor is already in SAP, the flow jumps straight to “SAP Vendor number added to invoice”. If the vendor is missing, the process routes to a “Fill out request for new Vendor Master Record form”, then “Staple request to invoice” and “Place invoice in internal outbox for new vendors”. After that a timer‑based intermediate event (internal outbox) hands the invoice to the “Master Data Entry Department”.  \\n\\nAt the Master Data Entry step an exclusive gateway splits the invoice into “Urgent” (24‑hour timer) or “Non‑Urgent” (1‑5‑day timer) paths; both converge on the same “SAP Vendor number added to invoice” activity. A second gateway asks how the invoice should be sorted: either “Invoices sorted by Vendor” or “Invoices sorted by amount”. Both branches merge at a third gateway and proceed to “Invoices entered into SAP system”, after which the process ends.  \\n\\nKey elements are the initial vendor‑existence decision, two timing gateways that enforce service‑level delays, and a sorting‑preference gateway that determines the final ordering before the SAP entry step."}
